  },
  {
    "uid": "C0419",
    "text": "Craft knowledge is included in a widely shared reference work. Practical making becomes part of learned knowledge despite censorship and disagreement.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2720,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-encyclopedic-craft",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0420",
    "text": "Craft enters the public account of knowledge",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2721,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-encyclopedic-craft",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0421",
    "text": "Cross-references let readers connect different subjects and practices. The structure supports more than one route through knowledge.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2722,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-encyclopedic-network",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0422",
    "text": "Knowledge joined by cross-reference",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2723,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-encyclopedic-network",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0423",
    "text": "A pattern that held in past observations is not logically guaranteed to hold in the next case. Hume asks what justifies making that further prediction.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2724,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-problem-of-induction",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0424",
    "text": "Past success does not guarantee the next case",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2725,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-problem-of-induction",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0425",
    "text": "Hume questions what justifies extending observed patterns beyond the cases already seen. Kant responds by asking what the mind contributes to make experience possible. His account is a philosophical response, not one experiment that settles the dispute.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2726,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-conditions-of-experience",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0426",
    "text": "Kant: the mind helps structure experience",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2727,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-conditions-of-experience",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0427",
    "text": "Social standing can demand more and more possessions. The older ideal of friendship and having enough challenges that demand: a higher status is not the same thing as a better life.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2728,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-sufficiency-against-status",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0428",
    "text": "Enough is not the same as higher status",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2729,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-sufficiency-against-status",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0429",
    "text": "Rights are claimed for people beyond inherited rank or privilege. Whether the claim is truly universal depends on whom law and practice include.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2730,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-universal-rights",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0430",
    "text": "A claim to rights beyond inherited rank",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2731,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-universal-rights",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0431",
    "text": "A declaration may invoke universal reason while women are denied the education used to develop it. Wollstonecraft turns that stated principle against the exclusion and unequal treatment of women.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2732,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-rights-for-women",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0432",
    "text": "Universal reason must include women",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2733,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-rights-for-women",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0433",
    "text": "A claim of universal liberty conflicts with enslavement. The testimony and actions of enslaved people expose that conflict, rather than leaving it as an abstract puzzle.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2734,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-rights-against-slavery",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0434",
    "text": "Universal liberty confronts enslavement",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2735,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-rights-against-slavery",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0435",
    "text": "Arguments are opened to criticism from a wider public. Broader discussion can challenge authority without guaranteeing equal participation.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2736,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-public-reasoning",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0436",
    "text": "An argument answerable to a wider public",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2737,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-public-reasoning",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0437",
    "text": "Mandeville argues that private motives condemned as vices can support public prosperity. The uncomfortable question is whether wealth created by such motives makes a society good.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2738,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-private-vice-public-benefit",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0438",
    "text": "Mandeville: private vice, public benefit",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2739,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-private-vice-public-benefit",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0439",
    "text": "Work is divided into specialized tasks, allowing more to be produced. Organization, not only machinery, can change a workshop's output.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2740,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-division-of-labour",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0440",
    "text": "Production divided into specialized tasks",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2741,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-division-of-labour",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0441",
    "text": "Specialized work may increase output while narrowing the worker's abilities and daily life. Greater efficiency is not the same as greater well-being.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2742,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-specialization-cost",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0442",
    "text": "More output can narrow the maker\u2019s life",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2743,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-specialization-cost",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0443",
    "text": "More trade and wealth do not automatically provide friendship, security or worthwhile activity. Comparing economic prosperity with the older ideal of a sufficient life keeps those different measures of success visible.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2744,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-prosperity-not-good-life",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0444",
    "text": "Prosperity and a good life can diverge",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2745,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-prosperity-not-good-life",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0445",
    "text": "Malthus argues that potential population growth can exceed growth in food supplies. This can create pressure, but it does not decide which response is fair.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2746,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-population-pressure",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0446",
    "text": "More offspring than available subsistence",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2747,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-population-pressure",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0447",
    "text": "A shortage describes a problem; it does not decide who should bear its costs. A policy still needs a separate justification.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2748,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-scarcity-and-justice",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0448",
    "text": "Scarcity does not settle who should bear it",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2749,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-scarcity-and-justice",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0449",
    "text": "Navigation and preserved food allow exchange over longer distances. Goods can travel farther because voyages can be located and sustained.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2750,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-long-distance-exchange",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0450",
    "text": "An enlarged world of exchange",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2751,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-long-distance-exchange",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0451",
    "text": "Long-distance exchange can depend on forced labour and political power. Technical improvements alone do not explain who benefits or who suffers.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2752,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-coercive-exchange",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0452",
    "text": "Exchange entangled with coercion",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2753,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-coercive-exchange",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0453",
    "text": "Workers are people whose abilities and lives matter, not only sources of output. A productive arrangement can still fail them.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2754,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-work-as-a-human-question",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0454",
    "text": "The maker is more than the output",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2755,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-work-as-a-human-question",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0455",
    "text": "The object is understood as a trace of former life. Comparing it with living organisms turns it into evidence about the past.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2756,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-organic-fossil",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0456",
    "text": "A fossil is a trace of former life",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2757,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-organic-fossil",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0457",
    "text": "The layers can be placed in order from earlier to later. This establishes a sequence without yet giving ages in years.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2758,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-relative-strata",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0458",
    "text": "A sequence of deposited worlds",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2759,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-relative-strata",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0459",
    "text": "Matching fossil sequences connects separated rock layers. A history can be reconstructed across more than one exposed cliff.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2760,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-correlated-strata",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0460",
    "text": "Separated beds, a comparable succession",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2761,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-correlated-strata",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0461",
    "text": "Streams erode rock and deposit sediment today. Those observed processes help explain similar traces preserved in ancient rock.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2762,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-process-history",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0462",
    "text": "Present processes can explain ancient traces",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2763,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-process-history",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0463",
    "text": "Tilted rock layers beneath younger level layers require several episodes: deposition, tilting, erosion and new deposition. The landscape records repeated change rather than one unchanged act of formation.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2764,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-cycles-in-rock",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0464",
    "text": "More than one making of the landscape",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2765,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-cycles-in-rock",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0465",
    "text": "Many layers and repeated changes require a long history. The evidence establishes an extended past without yet measuring exactly how many years it lasted.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2766,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-deep-time-world",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0466",
    "text": "A landscape needs a deep past",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2767,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-deep-time-world",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0467",
    "text": "Some kinds of animals no longer exist. A catalogue of life must therefore include a past that differs from the present.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2768,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-extinction-real",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0468",
    "text": "Whole forms of life have disappeared",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2769,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-extinction-real",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0469",
    "text": "Earth's history includes long-running processes and abrupt events. It need not be reduced to either constant slow change or one worldwide catastrophe.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2770,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-eventful-geology",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0470",
    "text": "Long processes and abrupt events",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2771,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-eventful-geology",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0471",
    "text": "Shared two-part names make records of species easier to compare. The names help investigation without making the groups beyond revision.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2772,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-named-species",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0472",
    "text": "Comparable names for living kinds",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2773,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-named-species",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0473",
    "text": "Living things vary with place, climate and altitude. Comparing these patterns connects classification with the conditions of life.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2774,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-geography-of-life",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0474",
    "text": "Life patterned by place and conditions",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2775,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-geography-of-life",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0475",
    "text": "Lamarck treats species as changing through use, disuse and inherited acquired changes. His proposed explanation differs from later accounts based on natural selection.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2776,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-transforming-species",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0476",
    "text": "Species can have changing histories",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2777,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-transforming-species",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0477",
    "text": "Breeding shows how small inherited differences can accumulate. Natural selection uses the comparison without requiring a breeder who plans nature's changes.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2778,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-selection-analogy",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0478",
    "text": "Small inherited differences can accumulate",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2779,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-selection-analogy",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0479",
    "text": "Offspring have inherited differences and face limited resources. These facts alone do not show which differences will leave more descendants; reproductive outcomes must also be compared.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2780,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-struggle-for-existence",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0480",
    "text": "Heritably varied offspring face limited resources",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2781,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-struggle-for-existence",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0481",
    "text": "Inherited differences that affect reproduction can become more or less common over generations. Natural selection describes this population change, not a rule that the strongest always win.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2782,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-natural-selection",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0482",
    "text": "Unequal reproduction changes a population",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2783,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-natural-selection",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  }
]